<title>USA: Northeast Utilities signs pipeline deal.</title>
<headline>Northeast Utilities signs pipeline deal.</headline>
<dateline>PORTLAND, Maine 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Northeast Utilities has reached a transmission agreement with the Portland Natural Gas Transmission System that includes purchasing a 5 percent stake in the pipeline project, pipeline officials said on Monday.</p>
<p>Northeast Utilities struck agreements with CoEnergy Trading Co and TransCanada Gas Services, a wholly owned unit of TransCanada PipeLines Ltd, two of the pipeline's shippers, to transport 60 million cubic feet per day of natural gas over the proposed pipeline.</p>
</text>
